1
00:00:02,449 --> 00:00:05,460
Wattle Bay Runners, Jodie speaking.

2
00:00:05,764 --> 00:00:09,840
Ben. Oh, hello.
I got this number from your website.

3
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:13,234
I'm thinking about joining
the club, and I was also

4
00:00:13,258 --> 00:00:16,272
hoping to find out about the
10km race you're organising.

5
00:00:16,585 --> 00:00:19,120
Lovely. You've come to the right person.

6
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:22,120
I'm the club secretary, so
I can help you with both.

7
00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:23,740
Can I grab your name first?

8
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,640
Ben. Ben Thursby.

9
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:30,620
I've only just moved here from Manchester,
so I don't really know anyone yet.

10
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:35,300
Well, a running club's a great way to
fix that. Have you been running long?

11
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,952
A few years, on and off. I did a
couple of half-marathons back

12
00:00:38,976 --> 00:00:42,232
home, but I've been a bit lazy
since the move, to be honest.

13
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:46,066
No dramas. Right, so
the club runs twice a week,

14
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:49,892
Tuesday and Thursday
evenings, and we start at 6.30.

15
00:00:50,209 --> 00:00:54,660
And where do you all meet? The website
mentioned the library car park, I think.

16
00:00:54,959 --> 00:00:58,420
Ah, yeah. Sorry.
The website's a bit out of date.

17
00:00:59,029 --> 00:01:01,608
We did used to meet at the
library, but then the council

18
00:01:01,632 --> 00:01:03,992
started charging for
parking there in the evenings.

19
00:01:04,639 --> 00:01:07,600
So, these days, we meet at
the pavilion in Norfolk Park.

20
00:01:08,019 --> 00:01:10,880
It's the building right next to
the cricket nets. You can't miss it.

21
00:01:11,149 --> 00:01:16,080
The pavilion next to the nets. Got it.
And is there a membership fee?

22
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,155
There is. It's an annual fee.
It was $65 last year, but we've

23
00:01:21,179 --> 00:01:25,212
had to put it up to $72, mostly
because our insurance went up.

24
00:01:25,494 --> 00:01:30,080
$72. That's still very reasonable.
Is there anything on top of that?

25
00:01:30,419 --> 00:01:33,276
Only if you want a club
singlet, and they're $15.

26
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:37,252
But that's entirely optional. Nobody
makes you wear one to training.

27
00:01:38,859 --> 00:01:42,774
Right. And what do I need to bring
when I sign up? Do you need a doctor's

28
00:01:42,798 --> 00:01:46,672
certificate or something? I know
some clubs back in England ask for one.

29
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:49,071
We used to, actually,
but not anymore.

30
00:01:49,095 --> 00:01:52,412
Now you just fill in a short
health questionnaire on the night.

31
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:57,318
What you will need to bring is a photo,
because we print everyone a membership card.

32
00:01:57,342 --> 00:02:00,872
And the card gets you 10% off at
the sports shop on the high street.

33
00:02:02,529 --> 00:02:06,411
A photo? Fine. I can sort that out.
Is there a group for people who are,

34
00:02:06,435 --> 00:02:10,491
uh, getting back into it? I don't want
to be left behind on my first night.

35
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:14,846
Everyone says that. Yes, there's
a beginners group on Tuesdays.

36
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:17,672
It's run by one of our
coaches, Gail Kerridge.

37
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,640
Sorry, was that Kerrigan?

38
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:26,740
No. Kerridge. K-E-R-R-I-D-G-E.

39
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:34,380
K-E-R-R-I-D-G-E. Thanks.
And she always takes the beginners?

40
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:38,837
She does now. She used to coach the
juniors, but she swapped over this year.

41
00:02:38,861 --> 00:02:41,892
And honestly, she's brilliant
with people who are nervous.

42
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,104
Before you hear the
rest of the conversation,

43
00:02:45,128 --> 00:02:47,812
you have some time to
look at questions 5 to 10.

44
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:57,740
Now, the race. The Charity
10k. When is it exactly?

45
00:02:57,764 --> 00:03:01,472
I saw a poster in a cafe that
said the 2nd of November.

46
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:07,808
Yeah, a lot of those posters went up
before we had to change it. It was going

47
00:03:07,832 --> 00:03:11,832
to be Sunday the 2nd, but the council's
resurfacing the coast road that weekend.

48
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:15,500
So we've moved it back a week.
It's now Sunday the 9th.

49
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:20,198
The 9th of November. That actually
suits me better. And where does it start?

50
00:03:20,222 --> 00:03:23,312
Somebody at work told
me it starts at the surf club.

51
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,940
It always has done, but the surf club's being rebuilt at the
moment. So this year, we're starting from the lighthouse, right

52
00:03:31,964 --> 00:03:36,256
at the north end of the beach. The finish is still in Norfolk
Park, though, so it's a point-to-point course rather than a loop.

53
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:39,121
The lighthouse. That should
be a nice view, at least.

54
00:03:39,145 --> 00:03:41,052
And how much
does it cost to enter?

55
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:45,408
That depends. For the
general public, it's $45, but club

56
00:03:45,432 --> 00:03:49,312
members get a decent
discount, so for members, it's $30.

57
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:50,920
Sorry, $13?

58
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:59,020
I wish! No, $30.3-0. So if you join before
you enter, you save $15 straight away.

59
00:03:59,499 --> 00:04:04,280
Well, that's another good reason to join.
And which charity does the money go to?

60
00:04:08,125 --> 00:04:12,029
Last year, it was the Animal Shelter, and the year before
that, it went to the Surf Lifesaving Club. This year,

61
00:04:12,053 --> 00:04:16,436
the committee voted for the local hospice. A few of our
members have had family there, so it means a lot to people.

62
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:19,204
That's a really good
cause. And, uh, how does it

63
00:04:19,228 --> 00:04:22,272
work on the day? Do I pick
up my number at the start?

64
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:31,285
That's how we used to do it, but the queues were terrible,
and people were missing the start. So now you collect your

65
00:04:31,309 --> 00:04:35,246
race pack the day before, on the Saturday, from the marina
office, down by the boat ramp. It's open from 9 till 4.

66
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:38,880
The marina office. So nothing's
given out on the Sunday morning?

67
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:42,737
Nothing at all, so don't leave it till
the last minute. There is a bag drop

68
00:04:42,761 --> 00:04:46,452
at the lighthouse, though, and we drive
all the bags back to the park for you.

69
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:50,800
Great. And is there anything for
people who finish? A medal, or...?

70
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:59,168
Everyone gets a medal, yes! We used to hand out
t-shirts as well, but, to be honest, hardly anybody wore

71
00:04:59,192 --> 00:05:03,306
them. So this year, every finisher gets a towel
instead. A proper beach towel, with the race logo on it.

72
00:05:03,330 --> 00:05:06,760
A towel? That's actually
useful, especially round here.

73
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,972
That was the idea. Oh, and
there are two water stations on the

74
00:05:10,996 --> 00:05:15,152
course, at 3 and 7 kilometres, so
you won't need to carry a bottle.

75
00:05:15,450 --> 00:05:17,550
Brilliant! Right, I'll
come along to the

76
00:05:17,574 --> 00:05:19,952
pavilion on Tuesday,
then, and join properly.

77
00:05:20,295 --> 00:05:24,860
Perfect. Don't forget your photo, and
say hello to Gail. She'll look after you.

78
00:05:25,215 --> 00:05:27,840
I will. Thanks very much, Jodie. Bye!

79
