88
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,200
Good evening, everyone.

89
00:06:15,201 --> 00:06:18,220
And thank you for coming
out on such a wet night.

90
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:22,380
I know some of you have come straight
from work, so I'll try to keep this brisk.

91
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:26,760
As you know, we're here to talk about
the Year 6 Outdoor Education Week,

92
00:06:26,895 --> 00:06:28,960
which takes place in
the first week of June.

93
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:32,960
Some of you will remember that
when the school first started these trips,

94
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:37,240
about 10 years ago, the main idea
was simply to get children more active.

95
00:06:37,705 --> 00:06:40,700
And fitness is still a very
welcome side effect, of course.

96
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:44,820
Other parents have said to me that it's
a useful step towards secondary school,

97
00:06:45,050 --> 00:06:46,840
and I'd agree that it helps with that.

98
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:50,023
But what the staff and I
really want from the week this

99
00:06:50,047 --> 00:06:52,812
year is for the children to
learn to manage without us.

100
00:06:53,155 --> 00:06:55,780
To pack their own bags,
keep track of their own kit,

101
00:06:56,045 --> 00:07:00,240
and make decisions in their groups without
an adult jumping in to sort everything out.

102
00:07:00,730 --> 00:07:03,560
That's harder than it
sounds, for them and for us.

103
00:07:04,110 --> 00:07:05,680
Now, some practical details.

104
00:07:06,110 --> 00:07:10,000
We're going back to Brackenside, the
centre in mid-Wales that we used last year,

105
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:12,620
so a lot of the staff
already know the site well.

106
00:07:13,095 --> 00:07:15,249
The children will again
be in activity groups

107
00:07:15,273 --> 00:07:17,152
of eight, each with
its own instructor.

108
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,996
We did ask whether the
groups could be cut to

109
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:22,432
six, but the centre
simply couldn't staff that.

110
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,019
What has changed is
that rather than coming

111
00:07:25,043 --> 00:07:27,232
home on the Wednesday,
as they did last year,

112
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:31,140
the children will stay a second night
and come back on the Thursday afternoon.

113
00:07:31,670 --> 00:07:35,200
The feedback we had was that one
night was over almost before it had begun.

114
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:38,020
The cost this year is £210.

115
00:07:39,010 --> 00:07:41,702
I know several families asked
whether there's a reduction

116
00:07:41,726 --> 00:07:44,052
when brothers and sisters,
or twins, go together.

117
00:07:44,490 --> 00:07:46,200
I'm afraid the centre doesn't offer one.

118
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,540
The coach isn't part of that figure either.

119
00:07:48,930 --> 00:07:52,640
The Parents Association has very
generously agreed to pay for it this year.

120
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:56,980
What we can do is let you split
the payment into three equal parts,

121
00:07:57,145 --> 00:08:00,460
in March, April and May,
rather than paying it all at once.

122
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,640
Just let the office know
which you'd prefer.

123
00:08:03,110 --> 00:08:05,580
And if the cost is a real
difficulty for any family,

124
00:08:05,895 --> 00:08:07,480
please come and talk to me privately.

125
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:09,640
Nobody will miss out for that reason.

126
00:08:10,219 --> 00:08:11,240
Mobile phones.

127
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:15,380
Last year, as some of you will
recall, we let the children bring them.

128
00:08:15,655 --> 00:08:19,660
They were collected when we arrived and
handed back for half an hour each evening.

129
00:08:20,570 --> 00:08:23,760
Honestly, it caused far more
homesickness than it cured.

130
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:27,500
So this year, please
don't pack a phone at all.

131
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,140
If you need to reach
your child, ring the centre,

132
00:08:30,390 --> 00:08:32,720
and we'll put photos on the
school blog every evening.

133
00:08:33,235 --> 00:08:34,880
Before you hear the rest of the talk,

134
00:08:35,225 --> 00:08:38,120
you have some time to
look at questions 15 to 20.

135
00:08:40,509 --> 00:08:43,740
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

136
00:08:44,229 --> 00:08:46,140
Let me run through the activities now,

137
00:08:46,230 --> 00:08:49,280
because each one needs
something slightly different from you.

138
00:08:49,745 --> 00:08:52,520
On the first full day, there's
cycling in the morning.

139
00:08:52,985 --> 00:08:55,060
Helmets and bikes are
provided by the centre,

140
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:57,940
and the children will be back
in plenty of time for lunch.

141
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:01,800
However, part of the route
goes along a quiet public lane,

142
00:09:02,099 --> 00:09:05,820
so this is the one activity the
centre won't let a child take part in

143
00:09:05,821 --> 00:09:08,060
without your signature
on the permission slip.

144
00:09:08,505 --> 00:09:10,040
Then canoeing on the lake.

145
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,722
Everyone is given a
wetsuit and a buoyancy

146
00:09:12,822 --> 00:09:14,900
aid, so they don't need
extra clothes for that.

147
00:09:15,624 --> 00:09:18,560
But their feet will get
soaked, without exception,

148
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:22,900
so they'll need a second pair of trainers
or old shoes to change into afterwards.

149
00:09:23,245 --> 00:09:25,420
Otherwise, they'll be
squelching about all day.

150
00:09:25,949 --> 00:09:28,080
The pond and stream study comes next.

151
00:09:28,505 --> 00:09:30,676
Some parents asked if
the children should bring

152
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,652
a torch for looking
under rocks and so on.

153
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:33,980
They don't need one.

154
00:09:34,295 --> 00:09:38,680
What I would say is that the mud at
Brackenside is a peculiar shade of orange,

155
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,540
and it does not wash out.

156
00:09:40,865 --> 00:09:42,874
Please send them in
something old that you won't

157
00:09:42,898 --> 00:09:44,752
mind putting straight
in the bin afterwards.

158
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:48,140
On the second evening, there's a
night walk up through the woods,

159
00:09:48,315 --> 00:09:50,100
which the children always love.

160
00:09:50,470 --> 00:09:54,000
The centre used to lend out lamps for
this, but they've stopped doing that now.

161
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,740
So every child must
bring a torch of their own.

162
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:00,840
It doesn't need to be anything
fancy, and please, not one that flashes.

163
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:03,720
The orienteering day is the longest one.

164
00:10:04,110 --> 00:10:07,680
The groups are out in Guern Forest
from morning until late afternoon,

165
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:09,980
which is too far to
come back to the centre,

166
00:10:10,279 --> 00:10:13,140
so for once, the kitchen
won't be providing a hot lunch.

167
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:17,000
Please make sure your child has sandwiches
and a drink with them that morning.

168
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:20,100
You might think they'd need
sun cream being out all day,

169
00:10:20,329 --> 00:10:23,840
but the centre has huge
supplies, so please don't send any.

170
00:10:24,245 --> 00:10:26,760
And finally, climbing on the indoor wall.

171
00:10:27,235 --> 00:10:29,820
The children's harnesses are
all checked by the instructors,

172
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,600
so you needn't worry about equipment.

173
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:35,860
But the climbing centre insists,
and this is their rule rather than ours,

174
00:10:36,109 --> 00:10:38,780
on having a list of any
medicines a child takes,

175
00:10:39,005 --> 00:10:41,380
especially inhalers, before that session.

176
00:10:41,845 --> 00:10:45,700
If that applies to your child, please write
it on the form that's going home tonight.

177
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,140
One last thing.

178
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:49,080
There's a small shop at Brackenside,

179
00:10:49,289 --> 00:10:51,420
and in the past, children
have taken pocket money.

180
00:10:51,625 --> 00:10:54,280
This year, the shop will
be closed for refurbishment,

181
00:10:54,639 --> 00:10:56,600
so they won't need any money at all.

182
00:10:56,945 --> 00:10:58,500
Right, I'll stop there.

183
00:10:58,880 --> 00:10:59,880
Are there any questions?

